---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';
import dpwh from '../data/generated/dpwh.json';
import fdp from '../data/generated/fdp.json';
import psa from '../data/generated/psa.json';
import { isoDate, num } from '../lib/format';

const refreshed = [psa.retrievedAt, dpwh.retrievedAt, fdp.retrievedAt].sort().at(-1) ?? '';
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="What BetterBauan is, how its figures are verified, and how to correct it."
>
  <section class="border-b border-line">
    <div class="wrap py-12 sm:py-16">
      <p class="kicker">About</p>
      <h1 class="display-xl mt-3 max-w-3xl">
        A record, <span class="text-brand">not a campaign.</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="lede mt-4 max-w-2xl">
        BetterBauan collects what Philippine national agencies already publish about the Municipality of
        Bauan, puts it in one place, and shows its work. It takes no position on any official, party or
        project.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap py-10 sm:py-12">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[1.35fr_0.65fr]">
      <div class="prose-block max-w-2xl text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
        <h2 class="font-display text-[1.5rem] tracking-tight text-ink">Why this exists</h2>
        <p>
          Bauan's public records are not secret. They are scattered: population in PSA's OpenSTAT, budgets
          and statutory filings in DILG's Full Disclosure portal, infrastructure contracts in DPWH's
          publication. Each is public on its own. None of them is arranged around the town.
        </p>
        <p>
          The municipality's own website, <span class="font-mono text-[0.85rem]">bauan.gov.ph</span>, did
          not respond when checked for this project. That is not unusual, and it is not a scandal — but it
          means the most reliable picture of Bauan is assembled from national records, not from the LGU's
          own site.
        </p>
        <p>
          So this site does the assembling in public. Every dataset is generated by a script in the
          repository, committed as JSON, and rendered at build time. Anyone can re-run the scripts and
          compare.
        </p>

        <h2 class="pt-4 font-display text-[1.5rem] tracking-tight text-ink">Independence</h2>
        <p>
          BetterBauan is volunteer-run and unaffiliated. It is not endorsed by, operated by, or funded by
          the Municipality of Bauan or any government agency. It carries no advertising, sets no cookies,
          and runs no analytics. The site is static except for one stateless assistant endpoint: a message
          you choose to send is passed to NYO, and no chat, account or audio is stored here.
        </p>
        <p>
          It is part of the{' '}
          <a href={SITE.directory} class="text-brand underline decoration-brand/30 underline-offset-2" rel="noopener">
            Better LGU directory</a
          >, a wider effort to give every Philippine local government a public, verifiable record.
        </p>

        <h2 class="pt-4 font-display text-[1.5rem] tracking-tight text-ink">The mark and the seal</h2>
        <p>
          The BetterBauan mark is the sun, municipal hall, green ridges and sea drawn for this project. It
          is a resemblance of the town, not an official insignia. The Sangguniang Bayan seal appears lower
          on the front page, with its ownership stated, only so readers can identify the government whose
          record this site follows.
        </p>
      </div>

      <aside class="space-y-4">
        <div class="card p-5">
          <h2 class="text-[0.72rem] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-muted">At a glance</h2>
          <dl class="mt-3 space-y-3 text-sm">
            <div>
              <dt class="text-muted">Scope</dt>
              <dd class="text-ink">Municipality of Bauan, Batangas</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt class="text-muted">Datasets</dt>
              <dd class="text-ink">{num(3)} — PSA, DILG, DPWH</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt class="text-muted">Records indexed</dt>
              <dd class="text-ink">
                {num(psa.barangays.length)} barangays · {num(fdp.summary.count)} filings ·{' '}
                {num(dpwh.summary.count)} contracts
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt class="text-muted">Last refreshed</dt>
              <dd class="text-ink">{isoDate(refreshed)}</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt class="text-muted">Built with</dt>
              <dd class="text-ink">Astro, static HTML, one edge endpoint for the assistant</dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
        </div>

        <div class="card p-5">
          <h2 class="text-[0.72rem] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-muted">Code & licence</h2>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
            Source is MIT-licensed. Written content and the generated datasets are CC BY 4.0 — reuse them,
            credit the agency that produced the underlying record.
          </p>
          <a
            href={SITE.repo}
            class="mt-3 inline-block text-sm text-brand underline decoration-brand/30 underline-offset-2"
            rel="noopener"
          >
            github.com/Arxenic/betterbauan
          </a>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="verification" class="scroll-mt-20 border-y border-line bg-surface">
    <div class="wrap py-12 sm:py-14">
      <h2 class="font-display text-[1.6rem] tracking-tight">How a figure earns its place</h2>
      <p class="lede mt-3 max-w-2xl">
        Three gates, applied in order. A figure that fails any one of them does not go on the site, however
        plausible it looks.
      </p>

      <ol class="mt-8 grid gap-8 sm:grid-cols-3">
        <li>
          <p class="font-display text-2xl text-brand/40">01</p>
          <h3 class="mt-1 text-[1rem] font-semibold text-ink">Provenance</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
            The figure must come from a tier A or B record — a machine-readable table published by the
            agency that produces it, or a primary document read by a person. Encyclopedia entries and news
            reports are leads, never citations. A tier C roster (the officials, for now) is labelled as
            reported and carries no derived numbers.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p class="font-display text-2xl text-brand/40">02</p>
          <h3 class="mt-1 text-[1rem] font-semibold text-ink">Reconciliation</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
            The dataset must agree with itself. All {num(psa.barangays.length)} barangay populations must
            sum to the municipal total; a contract's coordinates must fall inside the town. Where they do
            not, the build fails or the record is flagged.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p class="font-display text-2xl text-brand/40">03</p>
          <h3 class="mt-1 text-[1rem] font-semibold text-ink">Withdrawal first</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
            A disputed figure comes down before it is re-checked, not after. Reinstatement requires the
            same standard of evidence as publication. Git history records both moves.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ol>

      <div class="mt-8 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
        <div class="rounded-sm border border-line bg-paper px-4 py-3">
          <p class="text-[0.7rem] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-muted">Gate in practice · PSA</p>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
            The PSA build sums the barangay rows and compares them to the municipal row. A mismatch aborts
            the build instead of writing a wrong total.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-sm border border-line bg-paper px-4 py-3">
          <p class="text-[0.7rem] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-muted">Gate in practice · DPWH</p>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
            Contracts are kept only if the description names Bauan as a whole word. Coordinates outside the
            town are flagged, and pins are plotted only when the coordinate lands inside a barangay polygon;
            the unmapped remainder is disclosed rather than nudged into place.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-6 max-w-2xl">
        <Callout tone="warn" title="What is deliberately absent">
          <p>
            Municipal poverty incidence, the LGU's income class, and the ordinance index are missing. Each
            one is checked by someone as a matter of course and each one is easy to get subtly wrong. They
            stay off until a primary record is in hand. The 2025–2028 officials are published as a tier C
            roster; vote counts wait for the COMELEC proclamation — the{' '}
            <a href="/sources" class="text-brand underline decoration-brand/30 underline-offset-2">
              sources page</a
            > lists exactly what would unblock them.
          </p>
        </Callout>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="contribute" class="wrap scroll-mt-20 py-12 sm:py-14">
    <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-2">
      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-[1.5rem] tracking-tight">Correcting us</h2>
        <div class="prose-block mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          <p>
            A correction is more valuable than a compliment. If a figure here contradicts a document you
            hold, say which figure and attach the document — a scan, a link, a page number.
          </p>
          <p>
            Open an issue at
            <a href={SITE.issues} class="text-brand underline decoration-brand/30 underline-offset-2" rel="noopener">
              {SITE.issues.replace('https://', '')}</a
            >. Reports are triaged the same way records are: source first, then the fix.
          </p>
        </div>

        <h2 class="mt-8 font-display text-[1.5rem] tracking-tight">Contributing data</h2>
        <div class="prose-block mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          <p>
            The pipelines are plain Node scripts and a pull request is welcome. If an agency publishes
            something about Bauan and this site does not read it, that is a gap worth closing.
          </p>
          <p>
            Correction and verification policy is documented in the repository, so a contribution can be
            judged against a rule rather than a preference.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-[1.5rem] tracking-tight">Roadmap</h2>
        <ul class="mt-3 divide-y divide-line border-y border-line text-sm">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 py-3">
            <span class="mt-1.5 size-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-brand/50"></span>
            <span class="text-ink-soft">
              Extract the Statement of Receipts and Expenditures into typed revenue and expenditure lines,
              each with its sheet and cell.
            </span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 py-3">
            <span class="mt-1.5 size-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-brand/50"></span>
            <span class="text-ink-soft">
              Verify the 2025–2028 officials against the COMELEC proclamation, then publish vote counts
              alongside the roster.
            </span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 py-3">
            <span class="mt-1.5 size-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-brand/50"></span>
            <span class="text-ink-soft">
              Add locally funded projects from the Annual Investment Programme and the 20% development fund.
            </span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 py-3">
            <span class="mt-1.5 size-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-line-strong"></span>
            <span class="text-ink-soft">
              Municipal poverty incidence, once PSA's small-area estimates are retrieved and cited by page.
            </span>
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-4 text-[0.78rem] text-muted">
          Nothing on this list is promised with a date. A volunteer project that misses deadlines is worse
          than one that states its gaps.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
